#: ../../source/docs/using-DFU-to-load-bootloader.rst:5
#: f66c4d10a4e6412d9f9cc7048ce2fc1f
msgid "Loading a bootloader with DFU"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/using-DFU-to-load-bootloader.rst:7
#: 96e3f06a308c469ebae49a2db11b0852
msgid "This page describes how to load a new bootloader onto a STM32 based board (such as a Pixhawk1) via DFU. This is useful if you are either trying to bring up a new board or if you have a corrupted bootloader on an existing board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/using-DFU-to-load-bootloader.rst:13
#: 048f146e391447068915668b1da8cef1
msgid "What is DFU"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/using-DFU-to-load-bootloader.rst:15
#: 86f05e1bc4cb4c02b35ab8628b5a2e63
msgid "DFU is the \"Direct Firmware Update\" mode for some microcontrollers, most notably the STM32Fx series. It allows you to load a firmware (including a bootloader) over USB using widely available DFU utilities."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/using-DFU-to-load-bootloader.rst:21
#: 5317567363314f34b73bbb78b48241c6
msgid "Accessing DFU Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/using-DFU-to-load-bootloader.rst:23
#: e62035b22d374958ab15fb82d0940aa9
msgid "On many autopilots there is a separate \"boot\" button provided which will place the autopilot into DFU mode if powered while it is pressed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/using-DFU-to-load-bootloader.rst:26
#: 6dd8a56446a94665b2e7ff121f56534a
msgid "On many higher end autopilots no readily accessible button is provided and the autopilot must opened and a pad or cpu pin accessed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/using-DFU-to-load-bootloader.rst:29
#: c4107d1193714d7c9a3fd57a5370d874
msgid "On these autopilots DFU mode is entered by pulling the \"boot0\" pin high on the processor when it is powered on. On a Pixhawk1 this is done by pulling the \"FMU-BOOT\" pad on the top surface of the Pixhawk1 high. The FMU-BOOT pad is located between the buzzer and DSM/Spkt connectors on the Pixhawk1. On a 3DR Pixhawk FMU-BOOT is located between the switch and Telem2. You should pull it up to 3.3V, but in a pinch it does work to pull it up to 5V if you don't have 3.3V handy. The 3.3V supply on the switch is suitable for this."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/using-DFU-to-load-bootloader.rst:37
#: f0f57be50b304ddf9407ebfc524d1860
msgid "When the pin is pulled up apply power to the board (eg. plug in the USB connector) and the board should boot into DFU mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/using-DFU-to-load-bootloader.rst:41
#: 266b532a68df42cfa5c32bfbfaeff586
msgid "STM32Cube Programmer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/using-DFU-to-load-bootloader.rst:43
#: d57b6c80b2f5442798e8e35882a239b4
msgid "This utility is available for Windows, MACOS, and Linux and provides a simple GUI programmer. It is available at https://www.st.com/en/development-tools/stm32cubeprog.html ."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/using-DFU-to-load-bootloader.rst:45
#: ab43bf6989e64687bd99feb9ae8c01ec
msgid "You can download the appropriate bootloader from `here <https://firmware.ardupilot.org/Tools/Bootloaders>`__ and install it beginning at address 0x08000000."
msgstr ""

